ucational  inspiration and education many more than  you can realistically take advantage of  try not to be a lover of sights and  sounds for their own sakes and to chase  the easy quick fix of intellectual  gratification instead seek out in your  courses difficulty  embrace it of the vast array of courses  on offer and of the events over and  above the regular course offerings in  Yale College I'd like to call your  attention to three in the immediate  future and you'll be hearing about many  more the first event I want to call your  attention to you is an academic  conference on racism anti-semitism and  the radical right which we held on  September the 10th and 11th in the  Whitney humanities Center this is an  opportunity to hear national and  international academics address the  history of racism of anti-semitism of  fascism of white supremacy and other  radical white wing political movements  the second event I want to draw your  attention to you is the Wyndham Campbell  literary festival which ran strips and  timber the 13th to the 15th here you'll  have the opportunity to hear from the  recipients of the 2017 Donald wind and  sand M Campbell literary prizes come and  hear their craft and be inspired by the  example of their lives and writing and  their journeys and adventures at the  frontiers of human imagination and also  check out whether or not you're  interested in majoring in astronomy  check out the lightener observatory and  the planetarium which is open on tuesday  nights to enable you to scan the skies  to look at stars and to look at them  below so to conclude our collective work  as part of this university is serious  business and I know and we know that  you're ready for it  make us proud please class of 21 and  make yourselves proud thank you for  listening  thank you thank you so much professor  Greenwood for those moving words and  address and thank you all for just being  so great for for engaging with Yale so  positively over the past few days we're  so excited to have you here we're eager  to have you in our classes starting  tomorrow you know after this event your  colleges are going to formally welcome  you with a with a very nice dinner and  program and and before that before we  leave this hall today we're going to  introduce you to another very important  tradition our our song bright college  years you have the lyrics in hand we  have the the amazing yell glee club here  to share teach you the song together  with director Jeffrey Dalma and  professor Thomas Murray at the Oregon  the way this was going to work is that  the glee club is going to sing the first  verse and you can just listen and then  after that you will sing the first and  second verse together with the glee club  and at the end we're at the last line  for God for country for Yale you'll  you'll do this just follow what they do  okay so so yeah so thank you so much and  have a great year  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

